          "path": "_m/w/s/q/q/remains-of-taipei-prison-wall-wp/category-8.jpg",
          "filename": "臺北刑務所圍牆殘石.jpg",
          "caption": "Taipei Prison is a modern prison built by the Japanese people during the Japanese Colonial Rule in 1899～1904. The masonry of the wall was designed based on the modern prisons in Western countries. The stone of the demolished Tiapei City Walls in the Qing dynasty was resued to build the prison wall in order to reduce the construction cost.",
          "alt": "Taipei Prison is a modern prison built by the Japanese people during the Japanese Colonial Rule in 1899～1904. The masonry of the wall was designed based on the modern prisons in Western countries. The stone of the demolished Tiapei City Walls in the Qing dynasty was resued to build the prison wall in order to reduce the construction cost.",
          "width": 4592,
          "height": 3448,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
          "artist": "氏子",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E8%87%BA%E5%8C%97%E5%88%91%E5%8B%99%E6%89%80%E5%9C%8D%E7%89%86%E6%AE%98%E7%9F%B3.jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
          "sourceArticleId": "remains-of-taipei-prison-wall-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "wsqq"
        },
        {
          "path": "_m/w/s/q/q/remains-of-taipei-prison-wall-wp/category-9.jpg",
          "filename": "臺北刑務所圍牆近景.jpg",
          "caption": "Each layer of bricks was laid through stretcher-header bonds. The outer course of headers and the inner course of stretchers intersected in a \"T\" shape, and the inner course of headers and the outer course of stretchers also intersected in a \"T\" shape. The construction method ensured that the inner and outer course of bricks were laid with \"grooves\" and \"staggered joints\" to form a stable structure in which each layer of bricks was interconnected. \"Stucco paint\" made of granulated sugar and lime was also used to bond the bricks firmly.",
          "alt": "Each layer of bricks was laid through stretcher-header bonds. The outer course of headers and the inner course of stretchers intersected in a \"T\" shape, and the inner course of headers and the outer course of stretchers also intersected in a \"T\" shape. The construction method ensured that the inner and outer course of bricks were laid with \"grooves\" and \"staggered joints\" to form a stable structure in which each layer of bricks was interconnected. \"Stucco paint\" made of granulated sugar and lime was also used to bond the bricks firmly.",
          "width": 3424,
          "height": 3424,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
          "artist": "氏子",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E8%87%BA%E5%8C%97%E5%88%91%E5%8B%99%E6%89%80%E5%9C%8D%E7%89%86%E8%BF%91%E6%99%AF.jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
          "sourceArticleId": "remains-of-taipei-prison-wall-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "wsqq"
        },
        {
          "path": "_m/w/s/q/q/remains-of-taipei-prison-wall-wp/category-10.jpg",
          "filename": "臺北刑務所外牆近景.jpg",
          "caption": "The existing southern wall is about 180.8 metres long and 2 metres high （the upper wall has been damaged）. Sandstone from Dazhi was used to build the wall using the stretcher bond under the load-bearing structure （bottom：100cm wide；upper part：85 cm wide）. The stone is about 66～120 cm long and the cross section is about 20～26 cm square. Masonry is shown as follows.",
          "alt": "The existing southern wall is about 180.8 metres long and 2 metres high （the upper wall has been damaged）. Sandstone from Dazhi was used to build the wall using the stretcher bond under the load-bearing structure （bottom：100cm wide；upper part：85 cm wide）. The stone is about 66～120 cm long and the cross section is about 20～26 cm square. Masonry is shown as follows.",
